cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mujoco-hri-study: an experiment engine for human-robot interaction studies in MuJoCo"
message: "If you use this software in published research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Kite ML"
    website: "https://kiteml.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kite-ml/mujoco-hri-study"
abstract: >-
  mjhri is an experiment engine for human-robot interaction studies run in MuJoCo.
  A study is expressed as data — conditions, phase sequences, counterbalancing,
  survey instruments, tasks and geometric success criteria — and the engine walks
  participants through the protocol while recording an event log that doubles as
  the analysis dataset. It provides Williams-square counterbalancing, event-sourced
  protocol state with crash/refresh resume, renderer-agnostic survey instruments,
  scene-agnostic task scoring, keyboard teleoperation with damped-least-squares IK,
  and a dependency-light learning stack for closed-loop robot-teaching studies.
keywords:
  - human-robot interaction
  - MuJoCo
  - robotics
  - experiment design
  - counterbalancing
  - trust in automation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
